Requirements: 4   with obligations: 4

[task-01] The review report states, for every enumerated defect the pair-judgement stage
    was asked about, how many of that defect's pairs the run settled, how many were put
    to the judge, how many were dropped as not worth asking, and how many were skipped
    once the defect was covered. This holds for a defect the injection stage did not
    attempt, whose injection outcome is `not_mutable` or `not_attempted`, as much as for
    one it did.
    -> pair-judgement-defect-counts  [functional/explicit]
       The review report states, for every enumerated defect the pair-judgement stage
       was asked about, how many of that defect's pairs the run settled, how many were
       put to the judge, how many were dropped as not worth asking, and how many were
       skipped once the defect was covered.
    -> report-covers-unattempted-defects  [functional/explicit]
       The review report states, for a defect the injection stage did not attempt and
       whose injection outcome is `not_mutable` or `not_attempted`, how many of that
       defect's pairs the run settled, how many were put to the judge, how many were
       dropped as not worth asking, and how many were skipped once the defect was
       covered.

[task-02] The counts for such a defect are correct, not merely present. No edit was
    built for it, so none of its pairs was settled by the run and none was dropped or
    skipped on the strength of an edit: every one of its pairs is counted as put to the
    judge, including a pair the judge was offered and did not answer. The count of pairs
    put to the judge agrees wherever the report states it for the same defect.
    -> pair-counts-correct  [functional/explicit]
       The counts for such a defect are correct, not merely present.
    -> judge-pair-count-agreement  [invariant/explicit]
       The count of pairs put to the judge agrees wherever the report states it for the
       same defect.
    -> no-edit-built-for-it  [invariant/explicit]
       No edit was built for it, so none of its pairs was settled by the run.
    -> all-pairs-counted-as-put-to-judge  [invariant/explicit]
       Every pair is counted as put to the judge, with none dropped or skipped on the
       strength of an edit.
    -> include-judge-unanswered-pair  [functional/explicit]
       The count includes a pair the judge was offered and did not answer.

[task-03] A regression test is part of the deliverable: it renders a review holding a
    `not_mutable` defect and a `not_attempted` defect, each with pairs that went to the
    judge, and pins the exact counts the report states for each.
    -> render-review-with-two-defects  [functional/explicit]
       Render a review holding a `not_mutable` defect and a `not_attempted` defect.
    -> judge-pairs-for-both-defects  [functional/explicit]
       Render each of the `not_mutable` and `not_attempted` defects with pairs that went
       to the judge.
    -> pairs-went-to-judge  [functional/explicit]
       Each defect includes pairs that went to the judge.
    -> pin-exact-counts-report-states  [functional/explicit]
       Pin the exact counts the report states for each.
    -> regression-test-pins-exact-counts  [test_demand/explicit]
       A regression test asserts the exact counts the report states for each.

[exclusion-01] How pairs are routed between the run and the judge is unchanged; only
    what the report says about them is in scope.
    -> routing-unchanged  [functional/explicit]
       The change does not alter how pairs are routed between the run and the judge.

